          "id": "1765202485269",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765202485271_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Analyze the output {{$context.$nodes.WITHDRAW_REGISTRATION.$output}} \n\nIf the registration was successful, display \"Registration withdrawn from event {{$context.$nodes.GET_EMPLOYEE_EVENT_DETAILS.$output.Name}}\"\nElse display \"Withdraw registration failed for event {{$context.$nodes.GET_EMPLOYEE_EVENT_DETAILS.$output.Name}}\"\nDo not add any explanations. Display output in json format"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"Withdraw Status Schema\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"message\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"A message indicating withdraw status\"\n    },\n  \"event_name\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Event name\"\n}\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"message\",\"event_name\"]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1770069717463",
            "name": "ProcessAction",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "const str = $context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAction;\nconst payload = JSON.parse(str);\nconst action = payload. actionCode;\nlet array =[];\narray.push(action);\narray.push(payload);\nreturn array;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766388820642"
          },
          "code": "PROCESSACTION",
          "id": "1765436145520",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "ListActions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "LISTACTIONS",
          "id": "1765436334672",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765436334673_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are provided with event data below:\n\n {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.EventDetails}}\n\nYour task: Analyze this data to identify events that require immediate user decision or action regarding registration and readiness.\n\nIF actionable events are found:\n\nGenerate high priority actionable insights for the TOP 5 most relevant events only (or fewer if less than 5 require action). Focus on events that need attention based on factors such as:\n\nEvents where the user is \"Not Registered\" but fit the profile\n\nEvents requiring a readiness check based on user skills\n\nRegistered events that may require withdrawal\n\nHigh-interest events requiring detailed review\n\nFor each insight, use the following information:\n\ntitle: \"<Event Name> - <Action Type>\",\n\nshortDescription: \"<Concise explanation of specific action needed>\",\n\nactionText: \"<Action Button Text>\",\n\nfollowUpCommand: \"ora.Invoke(<actionName>, <somePayload>)\"\n\nAvailable Actions:\n\nGet Event Readiness Score: Use when the user has a skills profile compatible with the event topic but needs a fit assessment.\n\nTemplate: { \"title\": \"Get Event Readiness score for <EventName>\", \"shortDescription\": \"Based on your skills profile, get event readiness score\", \"actionText\": \"Calculate Event Readiness\", \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke('EventReadiness', somePayload)\" }\n\nRegister: Use when the user's status is strictly \"Not Registered\".\n\nTemplate: { \"title\": \"Register for <EventName>\", \"shortDescription\": \"Register for event\", \"actionText\": \"Register\", \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke('register', {\"EventNumber:$EventNumber})\" }\n\nView Details: Use when the user needs to inspect prerequisites or descriptions before deciding.\n\nTemplate: { \"title\": \"View more details for <EventName>\", \"shortDescription\": \"View More details about the event\", \"actionText\": \"View Details\", \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke('viewDetails', {\"EventNumber:$EventNumber}))\" }\n\nWithdraw: Use when the user is currently \"Registered\" for an event they no longer wish to attend.\n\nTemplate: { \"title\": \"Withdraw from <EventName>\", \"shortDescription\": \"Cancel your registration for this event\", \"actionText\": \"Withdraw\", \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke('withdraw', {\"EventNumber:$EventNumber}))\" }\n\nRequirements:\n\nReplace <EventName> with the actual name of the event from the data\n\nReplace <Action Button Text> with the text specified in the templates above\n\nReplace <somePayload> with the actual event ID or required parameters from the data\n\nPrioritize by urgency (upcoming start dates, registration deadlines)\n\nKeep shortDescription consistent with the templates provided above\n\nGenerate MAXIMUM 5 insights even if more events require action\n\nEach insight must be independently actionable\n\nIF no events requiring action are found:\n\nReturn an empty response with no data.\n\nIn addition, if there are multiple events the user is already successfully registered for that are coming up soon, add an additional low priority action with the title saying \"Review X upcoming registered events\" where X is the number.\n\nThe followUpCommand should be \"ora.Invoke(viewRegisteredEvents)\".\n\nOutput format: Return only the insight objects, nothing else."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "errorNodeId": "1770069717463",
            "name": "Summarize the Event Readiness"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZE_THE_EVENT_READINESS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1765486656611",
          "id": "1765489908360",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765489908362_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Using the *Event Readiness Scores* construct a well-formatted response to display the score, the rationale for the score and the pre-requisites recommended to be ready for the event.\n\n#Event Readiness Scores\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_EVENT_READINESS_SCORE.$output.output}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"Event Readiness Schema\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"score\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The overall event readiness score\"\n    },\n    \"rationale\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The rationale for the readiness score provided\"\n    },\n    \"pre-requisites\": {\n       \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"The pre-requisites that should be completed before event attendance.\"\n    }, \n \"skill-gap\": {\n       \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"description\": \"The skills that are required and helpful for the event.\"\n    }, \n  },\n  \"required\": [\"score\"]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_HCM_RECRUITING_ICCEMPLOYEEEVENTDETAILS",
            "errorNodeId": "1770069717463",
            "functionName": "getEmployeeEventDetails",
            "name": "Get Event Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765534035697"
          },
          "code": "GET_EVENT_DETAILS",
          "id": "1765532717047",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765532736945_1",
              "name": "EventNumber",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.PROCESSACTION.$output.result[1].EventNumber}}"
            }
